    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0794" n="784" xml:id="pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel J. Hart Caughey
                        to Colonel Marshall S. Carter
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-08-30">30 August 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1419. Because a CAF liaison officer, recently returned to Shanghai from Manila,
                    had knowledge of the temporary suspension delaying turnover of aircraft and
                    equipment under the 8 and ⅓ group program Reurad 98799,<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d474-f1"/> General McConnell<anchor n="24" xml:id="d474-f2"/> passed
                    the information to General Chou,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d474-f3"/> Commander in
                    Chief of the Chinese Air Force, probably yesterday afternoon.</p>
                <p>General Marshall has no objection to the proposed action in your last paragraph
                    of reference message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d474-f1" n="23" xml:id="d474-f1-content">
